 "10df90f0-7460-5f12-8581-b5f006e2d2a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365242 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{11}\\,m/s" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365242 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365242 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f110b675-f1c8-5f63-8220-fc65403fad04" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365243 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{14}\\,m/s" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365243 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365243 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2e95e064-0e7e-525f-a9b9-71fc8b392c06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365244 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{10}\\,m/s" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365244 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365244 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "60f55c07-f52c-5cbf-b071-44b4b630f272" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365245 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\sqrt{3}\\,m/s" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365245 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365245 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4fbc27f4-058f-5b3a-9cd6-5f66a1f934c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365246 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186365247 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365246 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163500" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365246 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365246 #edb/ref 1071 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis. When the displacement of $P$ from the origin is $x\\,m,$ the velocity is $v\\,m/s,$ the magnitude of the acceleration is $kx\\,{m/s}^{2},$ where $k$ is a positive constant, and the acceleration is directed toward $O.$ If $P$ has velocity $v=20\\,m/s$ at the origin and the particle is at rest when its displacement is $10\\,m,$ find the value of $k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365246 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "89d922d3-34d3-536f-bab1-5d011a22c471" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365246 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/cd/cd42eb74e5bba02951118c349a1b25f7193c39aa53f6504403918dfa984eb2c2.png)\n\nSince the acceleration of the particle $P$ has magnitude $kx\\,{m/s}^{2}$ and is directed *toward* $O,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-kx.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}),\n$$\n\nwe can rewrite our equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})=-kx.\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides of the above equation with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})\\text{d}x=\\int (-kx)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwhich gives the general solution\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}=-\\frac{k}{2}{x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nNow, since $v=20\\,m/s$ when $x=0\\,m,$ we can find the value of the constant $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =-\\frac{k}{2}{x}^{2}+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(20)^{2} & =-\\frac{k}{2}(0)^{3}+C \\\\ C & =200\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}=200-\\frac{k}{2}{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since $v=0\\,m/s$ when $x=10\\,m,$ we can find the value of the positive constant $k,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =200-\\frac{k}{2}{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2} & =200-\\frac{k}{2}(10)^{2} \\\\ 50k & =200 \\\\ k & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365247 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365248 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365247 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365247 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365247 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365247 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365247 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365247 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365247 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186365251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365247 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7eec898a-74f2-529d-b4bf-a5628b150053" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365248 #edb/ref 1080 "\\fra