of the velocity occur at the critical points of $v.$ Since the acceleration of the particle $P$ is $(10-2x)\\,{m/s}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=10-2x.\n$$\n\nTo find the moments where $v$ is a maximum, we need to solve $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=0$ and test each solution using the first or second derivative test.\n\nSolving $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10-2x & =0 \\\\ x & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the extremum of the velocity function occurs when $x=5\\,m.$\n\nWe now test the extreme value using the first derivative test. We summarize the necessary information in a table, shown below.\n\n| $x$ | $(0,5)$ | $5$ | $(5,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Test Point | $4$ |  | $6$ |\n| $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}$ | $2>0$ | $0$ | $-2<0$ |\n| $v$ | $↗$ | max | $↘$ |\n\nWe conclude that the velocity is maximized when $x=5\\,m.$\n\nNext, using the fact that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}),\n$$\n\nwe can rewrite our initial equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})=10-2x.\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides of the above equation with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})\\text{d}x=\\int (10-2x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwhich gives the general solution\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}=10x-{x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nNow, since $v=2\\,m/s$ when $x=0\\,m,$ we can find the value of the constant $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =10x-{x}^{2}+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(2)^{2} & =10(0)-(0)^{2}+C \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =10x-{x}^{2}+2 \\\\ {v}^{2} & =20x-2{x}^{2}+4 \\\\ v & =\\pm \\sqrt{-2{x}^{2}+20x+4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x,$ we have that $v(x)>0,$ so we can disregard the negative square root. Therefore,\n\n$$\nv(x)=\\sqrt{-2{x}^{2}+20x+4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the maximum velocity:\n\n$$\n{v}_{max}=v(5)=\\sqrt{-2(5)^{2}+20(5)+4}=3\\sqrt{6}\\,m/s\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365265 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365261 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365266 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365261 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365261 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365261 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186365264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365261 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "de8be0bb-c786-552b-8444-d92b5d0e42e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365262 #edb/ref 1080 "6\\,m/s" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365262 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365262 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9676d1bd-b5f6-576b-af89-b417c0b3f836" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365263 #edb/ref 1080 "4\\sqrt{2}\\,m/s" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365263 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365263 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "acd5375e-9e97-53b6-9073-a053c886f8bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365264 #edb/ref 1080 "3\\sqrt{6}\\,m/s" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365264 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365264 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a553426d-f0bb-5e6d-a4fa-349049cf240a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365265 #edb/ref 1080 "4\\,m/s" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365265 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365265 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6aa4d97d-b040-5b59-a4e2-7990a8d14150" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365266 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{5}\\,m/s" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365266 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 1759218604541